## A reaction wheel's power, transcribed from adcs-sim-core actuators.rs (Mex::apply, also a VSCMG's rotor): the
## steady power holding speed (the part's power_steady_W) plus the mechanical power of the motor's torque at the
## rotor's speed over the drive's efficiency (the product's eta, 0.8 as the engine flies it).
## The developer's transcription (S7.7), unsigned.
module wheelpower

## The power [W]: p_steady + |tm om|/eta.
fn wheel_power(p_steady: real[1] in 0 .. 5, tm: real[1] in -0.01 .. 0.01, om: real[1] in -1000 .. 1000, eta: real[1] in 0.5 .. 1) -> p: real[1]
    p = p_steady + abs(tm*om)/eta
end
